# Git

## Branches

- Branch flow: work branches → `develop` → `main`
- Create work branches from `develop` as `<type>/<short-description>` in English kebab-case (e.g., `feat/user-auth`)
- Do not commit directly to `develop` or `main`
- Do not merge into `develop` or `main` unless explicitly asked
- Merge work branches into `develop`, and `develop` into `main`, with `git merge --no-ff`, keeping Git's default merge message
- After merging a work branch into `develop`, delete it with `git branch -d`

## Commit messages

- Follow the Conventional Commits format
- Use one of these types: `chore` / `docs` / `feat` / `fix` / `refactor` / `style` / `test`
- Omit the scope
- Write the description in Japanese, ending with a noun rather than a verb (e.g., 「追加」, not 「追加する」)
- Omit the body if the subject line says it all
- When a body is needed, write it as a `-` bulleted list, with each item ending in a noun
- Omit incidental changes unrelated to the main purpose (formatting, reordering, minor comment tweaks, typo fixes, adding words to `cspell.json`, etc.)
